# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Watcher — environment configuration
#
# The app runs fully on rich MOCK data with NO key. To switch to live data from
# The Movie Database (TMDB), copy this file to ".env" and add ONE of the keys
# below. TMDB is free for personal use.
#
#   1. Create a free account:  https://www.themoviedb.org/signup
#   2. Go to Settings → API:   https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
#   3. Request an API key (choose "Developer", personal use).
#   4. Paste EITHER the "API Read Access Token" (v4, recommended) below,
#      OR the shorter "API Key" (v3).
#
# Use only one. The v4 token is preferred (sent as a Bearer header).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# v4 read access token (recommended)
VITE_TMDB_TOKEN=

# ...or v3 api key (alternative)
# VITE_TMDB_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud backup & cross-device sync (optional — Supabase, free tier).
# Leave blank to run local-only. To enable:
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
#   2. In the SQL editor, run the schema from SUPABASE_SETUP.md
#   3. In Project Settings → API, copy the Project URL and the anon public key
#   4. Paste them below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Video games (optional) — "on" once the `igdb` Supabase Edge Function is
# deployed with its Twitch secrets. See SUPABASE_SETUP.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_IGDB=
